# openPTT alert delivery configuration.
#
# Fill in the URLs below to activate alerts. Signup: https://healthchecks.io
# (free tier: 20 checks, email delivery, dead-man switch semantics).
#
# For each check, create it in healthchecks.io and paste the ping URL here.
# Recommended checks + schedules:
#
#   ALERT_HEARTBEAT_URL      A "simple" check pinged hourly by
#                            /etc/cron.hourly/ptt-heartbeat. If ping stops
#                            arriving, healthchecks emails you.
#
#   ALERT_DISK_URL           A "simple" check pinged daily by disk-check
#                            ONLY if usage is under threshold. Silence = alert.
#
#   ALERT_BACKUP_URL         A "simple" check pinged by backup.sh on success.
#                            Silence = backup failed.
#
#   ALERT_INCIDENT_WEBHOOK   Optional. If a check detects an active problem
#                            (murmur disconnected, disk >80%), POST here for
#                            immediate push. Point at healthchecks.io failure
#                            URL, ntfy, or a custom webhook. Leaving blank
#                            means we rely on the dead-man switch above.
#
# All alerts also mirror to journald (tag openptt-alert). If nothing here is
# configured, alerts silently no-op — no crash, just no email.

ALERT_HEARTBEAT_URL=""
ALERT_DISK_URL=""
ALERT_BACKUP_URL=""
ALERT_CERT_URL=""
ALERT_INCIDENT_WEBHOOK=""

# Disk-usage threshold for the daily check. Percent used.
DISK_ALERT_PCT=80
